  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Negate the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ At least one sequence is geometric.",
  "worked_solution": "Let $S$ be the set of all sequences. The given statement can be re-phrased as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists $s\\in S$ such that $s$ is geometric.\n\nIntroducing the existential quantifier, we get the following:\n\n$\\,$ $∃s\\in S,\\,s\\text{ is geometric}.$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∃s\\in S,\\,s\\text{ is geometric}) & ≡∀s\\in S,\\,¬(s\\text{ is geometric}) \\\\  & ≡∀s\\in S,\\,s\\text{ is not geometric}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich reads \n\n$\\,$ For all $s\\in S,$ $s$ is not geometric.\n\nor simply\n\n$\\,$ Every sequence is not geometric.",
